# Python Port Plan — Step 02 · The Registry

## Purpose

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/02_the_registry` to Python, producing
`week1_baseline/python/02_the_registry` that is behaviourally equivalent:
same `Registry` shape (`tool`/`dispatch`), same `UnknownToolError`, same
`example.rb` console output (modulo the accepted language-level divergences
already established in `01_struct` and one new one, below).

This is the third entry in the `docs/plans/python_port/<step>` series (see
[`context.md`](context.md) for the index). `01_struct_skeleton` is done; this
step adds `Registry` and `UnknownToolError` on top of it. `Config`, `Task`,
`Player`, `Tool`, `Message`, `Context` are all **unchanged** on the Ruby side
(confirmed with `diff` against `01_struct_skeleton`'s copies — byte-identical)
and get copied forward again, same as `01_struct_skeleton` copied them from
`00_config`.

